{"questions":[{"question_id":"1l31e917j","paperTitle":"IIT-JEE 2010 Paper 1 Offline","year":2010,"examDate":2010,"subject":"physics","chapter":"heat-and-thermodynamics","chapterGroup":"mechanics","topic":"thermodynamics-process","type":"mcqm","marks":4,"negMarks":2,"permalink":"pone-mole-of-an-ideal-gas-in-initial-state-a-undergoes-a-c-jee-advanced-physics-heat-and-thermodynamics-mjzbaua19hzjnpx9","content":"<p>One mole of an ideal gas in initial state A undergoes a cyclic process ABCA, as shown in the figure. Its pressure at A is P<sub>0</sub>. Choose the correct option(s) from the following:</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l31jr735/386a1b75-0e05-42d5-a07d-f2e4c1e7f2ab/4e850110-d124-11ec-b5bf-9d106fd05fc4/file-1l31jr736.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l31jr735/386a1b75-0e05-42d5-a07d-f2e4c1e7f2ab/4e850110-d124-11ec-b5bf-9d106fd05fc4/file-1l31jr736.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"IIT-JEE 2010 Paper 1 Offline Physics - Heat and Thermodynamics Question 34 English\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l31jr735/386a1b75-0e05-42d5-a07d-f2e4c1e7f2ab/4e850110-d124-11ec-b5bf-9d106fd05fc4/file-1l31jr736.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l31jr735/386a1b75-0e05-42d5-a07d-f2e4c1e7f2ab/4e850110-d124-11ec-b5bf-9d106fd05fc4/file-1l31jr736.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l31jr735/386a1b75-0e05-42d5-a07d-f2e4c1e7f2ab/4e850110-d124-11ec-b5bf-9d106fd05fc4/file-1l31jr736.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1l31jr735/386a1b75-0e05-42d5-a07d-f2e4c1e7f2ab/4e850110-d124-11ec-b5bf-9d106fd05fc4/file-1l31jr736.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1l31jr735/386a1b75-0e05-42d5-a07d-f2e4c1e7f2ab/4e850110-d124-11ec-b5bf-9d106fd05fc4/file-1l31jr736.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1l31jr735/386a1b75-0e05-42d5-a07d-f2e4c1e7f2ab/4e850110-d124-11ec-b5bf-9d106fd05fc4/file-1l31jr736.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"Internal energies at A and B are the same."},{"identifier":"B","content":"Work done by the gas in process AB is P<sub>0</sub>V<sub>0</sub> ln4."},{"identifier":"C","content":"Pressure at C is P<sub>0</sub>/4."},{"identifier":"D","content":"Temperature at C is T<sub>0</sub>/4."}],"correct_options":["A","B"],"explanation":"<p>The internal energy of one mole of an ideal gas at temperature T is given by U = 3RT/2. The process AB is isothermal i.e., T<sub>A</sub> = T<sub>B</sub> = T<sub>0</sub>, which makes U<sub>A</sub> = U<sub>B</sub>.</p>\n<p>The work done in the isothermal process AB is</p>\n<p>W<sub>AB</sub> = nRT ln(V<sub>B</sub>/V<sub>A</sub>)</p>\n<p>= nRT<sub>0</sub> ln(4V<sub>0</sub>/V<sub>0</sub>) = p<sub>0</sub>V<sub>0</sub> ln4.</p>\n<p>Information regarding p and T at C can not be obtained from the given graph. Unless it is mentioned that line BC passes through origin or not.</p>\n<p>Hence, the correct options are (a) and (b).</p>\n<p>Note:</p>\n<p>If we assume that the line BC pass through the origin. In the process BC, the slope V/T is constant. Thus, BC is an isobaric process (as V/T = nR/p, by the ideal gas equation). Thus,</p>\n<p>p<sub>C</sub> = p<sub>B</sub> = RT<sub>B</sub> / V<sub>B</sub></p>\n<p>= RT<sub>0</sub>/(4V<sub>0</sub>) = (RT<sub>0</sub>/V<sub>0</sub>)4 = p<sub>0</sub>/4.</p>\n<p>Apply the ideal gas equation for the states A and C to get</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -1.091ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"32.657ex\" height=\"3.46ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -1047.1 14434.6 1529.3\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D447\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D447\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(617,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D436\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D436\"></use></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1482.2,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(2538,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(220,477.2) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(536,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D436\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D436\"></use></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(1123.4,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D449\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D449\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(616,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D436\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D436\"></use></g></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(350,-345) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(536,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-30\"></use></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(939.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D449\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX